---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = '21 November 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Kshyv X Aum Social Publishing Engine"
  description="How Kshyv X Aum's owner-operated Pinterest publishing integration handles authorized account data, tokens, scheduling records, and requests for deletion."
>
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-neutral-950 text-neutral-50">
    <Nav />
    <main id="main-content" class="policy-page">
      <article class="policy-content">
        <header class="policy-header">
          <p class="eyebrow">Kshyv X Aum / Anyrvaan Studio</p>
          <h1>Privacy policy<span class="full-stop">.</span></h1>
          <p class="intro">
            A clear explanation of how the Kshyv X Aum Social Publishing Engine
            handles Pinterest account access. It is a private tool used by the
            account owner to schedule and publish their own devotional music and visual content.
          </p>
          <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        </header>

        <section aria-labelledby="operator">
          <h2 id="operator">01 / Who operates the tool</h2>
          <p>
            The Kshyv X Aum Social Publishing Engine is operated by Anirudh Khurana
            under the Kshyv X Aum creative identity and Anyrvaan Studio.
            For privacy questions, contact
            <a href="mailto:anyrvaan@gmail.com">anyrvaan@gmail.com</a>.
            The integration is intended for the operator's own Pinterest business account,
            not a public sign-up service or a tool offered to customers.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="access">
          <h2 id="access">02 / Pinterest information accessed</h2>
          <p>
            With the account owner's permission through Pinterest OAuth, the tool may access
            the authorized account's username or ID, its boards and board identifiers,
            and its own Pins and publication status. The tool needs this information
            to choose the correct board, create Pins, and confirm publication outcomes.
            It does not seek private information from unrelated Pinterest users.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="purpose">
          <h2 id="purpose">03 / How the information is used</h2>
          <p>
            The engine prepares and schedules approved Pins containing the owner's images,
            videos, titles, descriptions, and destination links to music or related content.
            The owner reviews and approves each destination before a live publish attempt.
            It also keeps local records of scheduling, approvals, attempts, and returned Pin IDs
            so the same item is not silently posted twice after a failed or uncertain request.
          </p>
          <p>
            Pinterest account data is not sold, used for third-party advertising,
            or used to train or fine-tune artificial-intelligence models.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="authentication">
          <h2 id="authentication">04 / Authorization and security</h2>
          <p>
            The integration uses Pinterest's official OAuth authorization process.
            It does not ask for or store the Pinterest account password.
            When connected, API access and refresh tokens are stored in a private,
            owner-controlled configuration location on the operator's computer,
            outside the public website and source repository. They are sent to Pinterest
            only as needed to perform authorized API requests.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="sharing">
          <h2 id="sharing">05 / Sharing and hosting</h2>
          <p>
            Approved Pin content and the necessary authorization information are sent to Pinterest
            through its API to carry out publishing. The publishing engine does not sell or
            distribute Pinterest account data to other businesses. This public policy page
            is hosted as part of anyrvaan.com; its hosting provider may process ordinary
            technical web-request information to deliver and secure the page.
          </p>
          <p>
            Pinterest's own handling of data is governed by its
            <a href="https://policy.pinterest.com/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="retention">
          <h2 id="retention">06 / Retention and deletion</h2>
          <p>
            Local scheduling and publication records are kept for as long as they are needed
            to operate the engine, audit publishing outcomes, and avoid accidental duplicate posts.
            OAuth credentials can be removed when the connection is no longer needed.
            For access, correction, or deletion requests relating to locally stored Pinterest
            integration information, email
            <a href="mailto:anyrvaan@gmail.com">anyrvaan@gmail.com</a>.
            Existing Pins on Pinterest may remain there until deleted through Pinterest.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="control">
          <h2 id="control">07 / Your choices</h2>
          <p>
            The account owner can disconnect the app by revoking access in Pinterest's connected-app
            settings. Revocation stops future authorized API access; locally held credentials should
            then be removed. The engine does not publish on behalf of other accounts without
            a separate, explicit authorization.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="updates">
          <h2 id="updates">08 / Updates</h2>
          <p>
            This policy may change if the integration's features or data-handling practices change.
            The date above will be updated to show the latest revision.
            Questions can be sent to
            <a href="mailto:anyrvaan@gmail.com">anyrvaan@gmail.com</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <div class="policy-footer">
          <a href="/">Return to Anyrvaan</a>
          <a href="https://in.pinterest.com/kshyvxaum/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kshyv X Aum on Pinterest</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy-page { padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 7rem) 1.5rem 6rem; }
  .policy-content { max-width: 48rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  .policy-header { padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem); }
  .eyebrow { color: #a1a1aa; font-size: .73rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .16em; }
  h1 { margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 8vw, 6.5rem); line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -.055em; font-weight: 400; }
  .full-stop { color: #60a5fa; }
  .intro { margin-top: 2rem; max-width: 39rem; font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.6vw, 1.2rem); line-height: 1.75; color: #d4d4d8; }
  .updated { margin-top: 1.5rem; color: #a1a1aa; font-size: .83rem; }
  section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 12.5rem) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2.5rem; padding: 2.6rem 0; border-top: 1px solid #303038; }
  h2 { color: #f4f4f5; font-size: .85rem; letter-spacing: .02em; line-height: 1.55; font-weight: 500; }
  section p { grid-column: 2; margin: 0; font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.85; color: #b8b8c1; }
  section p + p { margin-top: -.65rem; }
  a { color: #c4dcff; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: #6f819e; text-underline-offset: .25em; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  a:hover { color: #fff; text-decoration-color: #fff; }
  .policy-footer { border-top: 1px solid #303038; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.5rem 2.5rem; padding-top: 2.5rem; font-size: .85rem; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    section { display: block; padding: 2rem 0; }
    section p { margin-top: 1rem; }
    section p + p { margin-top: 1rem; }
  }
</style>
